 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:09:53.599174Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, a lease provision is void only if it conflicts with the Act. While the Act voids \"no-pet\" clauses, it does not shield a tenant from liability for property damage caused by their pet due to the tenant's negligence. \n\nSection 34 of the Act explicitly makes a tenant responsible for the repair of \"undue damage\" to the rental unit or residential complex caused by the \"wilful or negligent conduct of the tenant.\" Because carelessness constitutes negligence, requiring the tenant to pay to repair undue damage caused by their dog as a result of the tenant's carelessness aligns directly with the tenant's statutory obligation.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 34",
